### `/home/cis/windows/realstate/components/motion/scroll-reveal.tsx` (118 lines, `"use client"`) — the only GSAP file
**Imports:** `useEffect, useRef`; `useReducedMotionPreference`. GSAP is dynamic-only.
**Exports:** `ScrollReveal({ children, parallax = false })`, `RevealLine({ children })`.

```tsx
const [{ gsap }, { ScrollTrigger }] = await Promise.all([
  import("gsap"),
  import("gsap/ScrollTrigger"),
]);
gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);
const context = gsap.context(() => { … }, element);
// cleanup: context.revert()
```
Line reveal — queries `[data-reveal-line]` (emitted by `RevealLine`):
```tsx
const reveal = gsap.from(lines, {
  yPercent: 110, opacity: 0, duration: 0.9, ease: "power3.out", stagger: 0.08,
  scrollTrigger: { trigger: element, start: "top 78%", once: true },
});
```
Plus a **2500ms safety timer** — the notable defensive pattern here:
```tsx
safety = window.setTimeout(() => {
  if (!reveal.scrollTrigger?.isActive && reveal.progress() === 0) {
    reveal.progress(1);
  }
}, 2500);
```
Optional parallax on `[data-parallax]`: `gsap.to(target, { yPercent: -12, ease: "none", scrollTrigger: { trigger: element, start: "top bottom", end: "bottom top", scrub: 0.6 } })`.

`RevealLine` markup: `<span className="block overflow-hidden"><span data-reveal-line className="block">{children}</span></span>` — the mask wrapper for the `yPercent: 110` slide.

**Only one call site in the whole app**: `app/page.tsx:77–93` (two `RevealLine`s in the "Currently building" H2). No `parallax` prop is ever passed anywhere, and no `[data-parallax]` element exists in the repo — the parallax branch is unexercised.

**GSAP↔Lenis are NOT connected.** There is no `lenis.on("scroll", ScrollTrigger.update)` and no `ScrollTrigger.scrollerProxy`. GSAP relies on native scroll position, which happens to work because Lenis 1.x drives `window.scrollTo`, but there's no explicit wiring. Worth adding deliberately for any scrub-heavy expansion.

