  subscribe,                                  // matchMedia change listener
  () => window.matchMedia(QUERY).matches,     // client snapshot
  () => false,                                // server snapshot
);
```
This is the single source of truth read by: `hero-canvas`, `scroll-frame-sequence`, `master-plan`, `fade-in-view`, `scroll-reveal`, `lenis-provider`. **Everything you add should read this hook.**

### `/home/cis/windows/realstate/components/providers/lenis-provider.tsx` (42 lines, `"use client"`)
**Imports:** `useEffect`; `Lenis from "lenis"`; `"lenis/dist/lenis.css"`; `useReducedMotionPreference`.
**Export:** `LenisProvider()` — renders `null`, mounted at `app/layout.tsx:83`.

```tsx
if (reducedMotion) return;
const isTouch = window.matchMedia("(pointer: coarse)").matches;
if (isTouch) return;
const lenis = new Lenis({ lerp: 0.1, wheelMultiplier: 1 });
let frame = 0;
const raf = (time: number) => { lenis.raf(time); frame = requestAnimationFrame(raf); };
frame = requestAnimationFrame(raf);
return () => { cancelAnimationFrame(frame); lenis.destroy(); };
```
**No Lenis instance is exposed** — no context, no ref, no `useLenis()`. Any component that needs scroll progress (like `ScrollFrameSequence`) has to sample `getBoundingClientRect()` in its own rAF loop. If the overhaul wants scroll-linked 3D, this provider needs to publish the instance.

Related CSS: `app/globals.css:154-158` sets `html { scroll-behavior: auto; }` for Lenis, and `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` at line 285 clamps all animation/transition durations to `0.01ms !important`.

